triggers:
  - id: black-death
    name: Black Death reaches Europe
    date: 1347-10
    row: 11
    tags: [health, society]
    description: A third of Europe died; scarce labour raised wages and the value of labour-saving devices.
  - id: gutenberg-bible
    name: Gutenberg Bible printed
    date: 1455-01
    row: 13
    tags: [knowledge]
    description: The first major book printed with movable metal type in Europe.
  - id: columbus-voyage
    name: Columbus reaches the Americas
    date: 1492-10
    row: 15
    tags: [transport, economy]
    description: A voyage west that joined two hemispheres' trade, crops and diseases.
  - id: watt-condenser
    name: Watt's separate condenser patent
    date: 1769-01
    row: 1
    tags: [energy]
    description: A condenser apart from the cylinder made the steam engine efficient enough to drive mills.
  - id: jenner-smallpox
    name: Jenner's smallpox inoculation
    date: 1796-05
    row: 5
    tags: [health]
    description: Edward Jenner inoculated a boy with cowpox and showed he was protected from smallpox.
  - id: wright-flyer
    name: Wright brothers' first flight
    date: 1903-12
    row: 27
    tags: [transport]
    description: Twelve seconds of controlled, powered flight at Kitty Hawk.
  - id: penicillin
    name: Fleming notices penicillin
    date: 1928-09
    row: 17
    tags: [health]
    description: A mould killing the bacteria around it on a forgotten culture plate.
  - id: chicago-pile
    name: Chicago Pile-1 goes critical
    date: 1942-12
    row: 29
    tags: [energy]
    description: The first self-sustaining nuclear chain reaction.
  - id: sputnik
    name: Sputnik 1
    date: 1957-10
    row: 11
    tags: [transport, knowledge]
    description: The first artificial satellite, and the start of the space race.
  - id: code-of-hammurabi
    name: Code of Hammurabi
    date: -1754-01
    row: 13
    tags: [society]
    description: Babylonian laws carved on a stele for anyone to read.
  - id: bronze-age-collapse
    name: Late Bronze Age collapse
    date: -1177-01
    row: 3
    tags: [society, materials]
    description: Trade in tin failed with the palace states, and iron took its place.
  - id: library-of-alexandria
    name: Library of Alexandria founded
    date: -0285-01
    row: 7
    tags: [knowledge]
    description: A royal library that set out to hold every book in the world.
  - id: cai-lun-paper
    name: Cai Lun presents paper to the emperor
    date: 0105-01
    row: 1
    tags: [knowledge]
    description: Paper made from bark, hemp and rags, reported to the Han court.
